        "original_id": "a5a25b5c-dbc0-5c56-a763-e88ca459d27a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Klemzig Interchange, Adelaide, Klemzig, Essen, South Australia\n- Systems: O-Bahn Busway, O-Bahn system, bus rapid transit\n- Companies: Daimler-Benz\n\nFacts:\n- The O-Bahn system was conceived by Daimler-Benz to let buses avoid traffic congestion by sharing tram tunnels in Essen, Germany.\n- The O-Bahn Busway is a guided busway within the bus rapid transit system that serves the northeastern suburbs of Adelaide, South Australia.\n- Klemzig Interchange, previously called Klemzig Station, is an interchange on the O-Bahn Busway in the suburb of Klemzig in Adelaide, South Australia.",
